{"book":40,"chapter":1,"context":{"chapter":1,"title":"The Family Line of the Messiah","summary":"Matthew traces Jesus' family from Abraham through David to Joseph, then tells how Joseph, warned in a dream, takes pregnant Mary as his wife and names the child Jesus.","background":"Family records established who belonged to Israel and who could claim David's throne. Matthew arranges the names in three groups of fourteen (v. 17) and, as ancient genealogies often did, leaves some out: three kings between Joram and Ozias (Uzziah) are skipped.","customs":[{"term":"Betrothal","verses":"1:18-19","note":"Betrothal was far stronger than an engagement. The couple were legally bound and called husband and wife before living together, so ending it took a formal divorce, which is why Joseph planned to 'put her away privily.'"}],"watchFor":["Four women besides Mary appear in the list: Tamar, Rahab, Ruth and 'her that had been the wife of Urias' (vv. 3–6).","The name Jesus is explained: 'he shall save his people from their sins' (v. 21)."],"connections":["Isaiah 7:14","Ruth 4:18-22","2 Samuel 7:12-16","1 Chronicles 3:10-17"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["Βίβλος","Biblos","G976","N-NSF","[The] book"],["γενέσεως","geneseōs","G1078","N-GSF","of [the] genealogy"],["Ἰησοῦ","Iēsou","G2424","N-GSM-P","of Jesus"],["Χριστοῦ","Christou","G5547","N-GSM-T","Christ"],["υἱοῦ","huiou","G5207","N-GSM","son"],["Δαυὶδ","Dauid","G1138","N-GSM-P","of David"],["υἱοῦ","huiou","G5207","N-GSM","son"],["Ἀβραάμ","Abraam","G11","N-GSM-P","of Abraham"]],"x":[[1022018,1022018,30],[45001003,45001003,28],[48003016,48003016,25],[66022016,66022016,21],[19132011,19132011,20],[24023005,24023005,15],[23011001,23011001,12],[23009006,23009007,11],[42001031,42001032,11],[1012003,1012003,10]],"xn":15},"2":{"w":[["Ἀβραὰμ","Abraam","G11","N-NSM-P","Abraham"],["ἐγέννησεν","egennēsen","G1080","V-AAI-3S","begat"],["τὸν","ton","G3588","T-ASM","<the>"],["Ἰσαάκ·","Isaak","G2464","N-ASM-P","Isaac"],["Ἰσαὰκ","Isaak","G2464","N-NSM-P","Is