"V-AAI-3S","(s)he called"],["τὸ","to","G3588","T-ASN","the"],["ὄνομα","onoma","G3686","N-ASN","name"],["αὐτοῦ","autou","G846","P-GSM","of Him"],["Ἰησοῦν","Iēsoun","G2424","N-ASM-P","Jesus"]],"x":[[42002021,42002021,4],[2013002,2013002,3],[2022029,2022029,3],[40001021,40001021,3],[42002007,42002007,3]],"xn":5}},"people":[{"id":"jesus_905","name":"Jesus","also":"Immanuel, Emmanuel, Messiah, Shiloh, Christ, Jesus Christ, Messias","summary":"Anointed, the Greek translation of the Hebrew word rendered “Messiah”, the official title of our Lord, occurring five hundred and fourteen times in the New Testament.","verses":1831,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Mary","v":[1,16,17,18,21,22,23,25]},{"id":"david_994","name":"David","also":"","summary":"Beloved, the eighth and youngest son of Jesse, a citizen of Bethlehem. His father seems to have been a man in humble life. His mother’s name is not recorded.","verses":896,"father":"Jesse","mother":"","v":[1,6,17,20]},{"id":"abraham_58","name":"Abraham","also":"Abram","summary":"Father of a multitude, son of Terah, named (Gen. 11:27) before his older brothers Nahor and Haran, because he was the heir of the promises. Till the age of seventy, Abram sojourned among his kindred in his native country of Chaldea.","verses":277,"father":"Terah","mother":"","v":[1,2,17]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[2]},{"id":"isaac_616","name":"Isaac","also":"","summary":"The only son of Abraham by Sarah. He was the longest lived of the three patriarchs (Gen. 21:1-3).","verses":123,"father":"Abraham","mother":"Sarah","v":[2]},{"id":"pharez_2338","name":"Pharez","also":"Phares, Perez","summary":"Pharez,, breach, the son of Judah (Neh. 11:4). “The chief of all the captains of the host for the first month” in the reign of David was taken from his family (1 Chr. 27:3).","verses":15,"father":"Judah","mother":"Tamar","v":[3]},{"id":"hezron_1520","name":"Hezron","also":"Esrom","summary":"The older of the two sons of Pharez (Gen. 46:12).","verses":13,"father":"Pharez","mother":"","v":[3]},{"id":"zerah_2984","name":"Zerah","also":"Zara, Zarah","summary":"A son of Tamar (Gen. 38:30); called also Zara (Matt. 1:3).","verses":12,"father":"Judah","mother":"Tamar","v":[3]},{"id":"tamar_2821","name":"Tamar","also":"Thamar","summary":"The daughter-in-law of Judah, to whose eldest son, Er, she was married (Gen. 38:6). After her husband’s death, she was married to Onan, his brother (8), and on his death, Judah promised to her that his third son, Shelah, would become her husband.","verses":7,"father":"","mother":"","v":[3]},{"id":"ram_2391","name":"Ram","also":"Aram","summary":"The son of Hezron, and one of the ancestors of the royal line (Ruth 4:19).","verses":6,"father":"Hezron","mother":"","v":[3,4]},{"id":"amminadab_228","name":"Amminadab","also":"Aminadab","summary":"The father of Nahshon, who was chief of the tribe of Judah (Num. 1:7; 2:3; 7:12, 17; 10:14).","verses":11,"father":"Ram","mother":"","v":[4]},{"id":"nahshon_2144","name":"Nahshon","also":"Naasson, Naashon","summary":"Sorcerer, the son of Aminadab, and prince of the children of Judah at the time of the first numbering of the tribes in the wilderness (Ex. 6:23).","verses":11,"father":"Amminadab","mother":"","v":[4]},{"id":"salmon_2463","name":"Salmon","also":"Salma","summary":"Shady; or Zalmon, a hill covered with dark forests, south of Shechem, from which Abimelech and his men gathered wood to burn that city (Judg. 9:48).","verses":6,"father":"Nahshon","mother":"","v":[4,5]},{"id":"jesse_903","name":"Jesse","also":"","summary":"Firm, or a gift, a son of Obed, the son of Boaz and Ruth (Ruth 4:17, 22; Matt. 1:5, 6; Luke 3:32). He was the father of eight sons, the youngest of whom was David (1 Sam. 17:12).","verses":44,"father":"Obed","mother":"","v":[5,6]},{"id":"boaz_519","name":"Boaz","also":"Booz","summary":"The husband of Ruth, a wealthy Bethlehemite. By the “levirate law” the duty devolved on him of marrying Ruth the Moabitess (Ruth 4:1-13).","verses":24,"father":"Salmon","mother":"Rachab","v":[5]},{"id":"ruth_2450","name":"Ruth","also":"","summary":"A friend, a Moabitess, the wife of Mahlon, whose father, Elimelech, had settled in the land of Moab. On the death of Elimelech and Mahlon, Naomi came with Ruth, her daughter-in-law, who refused to leave her, to Bethlehem, the old home from which Elimelech had migrated.","verses":13,"father":"","mother":"","v":[5]},{"id":"obed_2228","name":"Obed","also":"","summary":"A son of Boaz and Ruth (Ruth 4:21, 22), and the grandfather of David (Matt. 1:5).","verses":6,"father":"Boaz","mother":"Ruth","v":[5]},{"id":"rachab_2385","name":"Rachab","also":"","summary":"Rahab, a name found in the genealogy of our Lord (Matt. 1:5).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[5]},{"id":"solomon_2762","name":"Solomon","also":"Jedidiah","summary":"Peaceful, (Heb. Shelomoh), David’s second son by Bathsheba, i.e., the first after their legal marriage (2 Sam. 12). He was probably born about B.C. 1035 (1 Chr. 22:5; 29:1).","verses":273,"father":"David","mother":"Bathsheba","v":[6,7]},{"id":"uriah_2898","name":"Uriah","also":"Urias","summary":"A Hittite, the husband of Bathsheba, whom David first seduced, and then after Uriah’s death married. He was one of the band of David’s “mighty men.”","verses":22,"father":"","mother":"","v":[6]},{"id":"asa_318","name":"Asa","also":"","summary":"Physician, son of Abijah and grandson of Rehoboam, was the third king of Judah. He was zealous in maintaining the true worship of God, and in rooting all idolatry, with its accompanying immoralities, out of the land (1 Kings 15:8-14).","verses":53,"father":"Abijah","mother":"","v":[7,8]},{"id":"rehoboam_2412","name":"Rehoboam","also":"Roboam","summary":"He enlarges the people, the successor of Solomon on the throne, and apparently his only son. He was the son of Naamah “the Ammonitess,” some well-known Ammonitish princess (1 Kings 14:21; 2 Chr. 12:13).","verses":42,"father":"Solomon","mother":"Naamah","v":[7]},{"id":"abijah_38","name":"Abijah","also":"Abijam, Abia","summary":"The son of Rehoboam, whom he succeeded on the throne of Judah (1 Chr. 3:10). He is also called Abijam (1 Kings 14:31; 15:1-8). He began his three years’ reign (2 Chr. 12:16; 13:1, 2) with a strenuous but unsuccessful effort to bring back the ten tribes to their allegiance.","verses":20,"father":"Rehoboam","mother":"Maachah","v":[7]},{"id":"jehoshaphat_808","name":"Jehoshaphat","also":"Josaphat","summary":"The son and successor of Asa, king of Judah. After fortifying his kingdom against Israel (2 Chr. 17:1, 2), he set himself to cleanse the land of idolatry (1 Kings 22:43).","verses":69,"father":"Asa","mother":"Azubah","v":[8]},{"id":"uzziah_375","name":"Uzziah","also":"Azariah, Ozias","summary":"One of Amaziah’s sons, whom the people made king of Judah in his father’s stead (2 Kings 14:21; 2 Chr. 26:1). His long reign of about fifty-two years was “the most prosperous excepting that of Jehosaphat since the time of Solomon.”","verses":33,"father":"Amaziah","mother":"Jecoliah","v":[8,9]},{"id":"jehoram_803","name":"Jehoram","also":"Joram","summary":"The eldest son and successor of Jehoshaphat, king of Judah. He reigned eight years (B.C. 892-885) alone as king of Judah, having been previously for some years associated with his father (2 Chr. 21:5, 20; 2 Kings 8:16).","verses":16,"father":"Jehoshaphat","mother":"","v":[8]},{"id":"hezekiah_1512","name":"Hezekiah","also":"Ezekias","summary":"Son of Ahaz (2 Kings 18:1; 2 Chr. 29:1), whom he succeeded on the throne of the kingdom of Judah. He reigned twenty-nine years (B.C. 726-697).","verses":116,"father":"Ahaz","mother":"Abijah","v":[9,10]},{"id":"ahaz_118","name":"Ahaz","also":"Achaz","summary":"The son and successor of Jotham, king of Judah (2 Kings 16; Isa. 7-9; 2 Chr. 28). He gave himself up to a life of wickedness and idolatry. Notwithstanding the remonstrances and warnings of Isaiah, Hosea, and Micah, he appealed for help against Rezin, king of Damascus, and Pekah, king of Israel, who threatened Jerusalem, to Tiglath-pileser, the king of Assyria, to the great injury of his kingdom and his own humilating subjection to the Assyrians (2 Kings 16:7, 9; 15:29).","verses":37,"father":"Jotham","mother":"","v":[9]},{"id":"jotham_1735","name":"Jotham","also":"Joatham","summary":"The son and successor of Uzziah on the throne of Judah. As during his last years Uzziah was excluded from public life on account of his leprosy, his son, then twenty-five years of age, administered for seven years the affairs of the kingdom in his father’s stead (2 Chr. 26:21, 23; 27:1).","verses":20,"father":"Uzziah","mother":"Jerushah","v":[9]},{"id":"josiah_1730","name":"Josiah","also":"Josias","summary":"Healed by Jehovah, or Jehovah will support. The son of Amon, and his successor on the throne of Judah (2 Kings 22:1; 2 Chr. 34:1). His history is contained in 2 Kings 22, 23.","verses":49,"father":"Amon","mother":"Jedidah","v":[10,11]},{"id":"manasseh_1930","name":"Manasseh","also":"Manasses","summary":"The elder of the two sons of Joseph. He and his brother Ephraim were afterwards adopted by Jacob as his own sons (48:1).","verses":24,"father":"Hezekiah","mother":"Hephzi-bah","v":[10]},{"id":"amon_236","name":"Amon","also":"","summary":"The son of Manasseh, and fourteenth king of Judah. He restored idolatry, and set up the images which his father had cast down.","verses":15,"father":"Manasseh","mother":"Meshullemeth","v":[10]},{"id":"jehoiachin_791","name":"Jehoiachin","also":"Jeconiah, Coniah, Jechonias","summary":"Succeeded his father Jehoiakin (B.C. 599) when only eight years of age, and reigned for one hundred days (2 Chr. 36:9). He is also called Jeconiah (Jer. 24:1; 27:20, etc.), and Coniah (22:24; 37:1).","verses":21,"father":"Jehoiakim","mother":"Nehushta","v":[11,12]},{"id":"zerubbabel_3054","name":"Zerubbabel","also":"Sheshbazzar, Zorobabel","summary":"The seed of Babylon, the son of Salathiel or Shealtiel (Hag. 1:1; Zorobabel, Matt. 1:12); called also the son of Pedaiah (1 Chr. 3:17-19), i.e., according to a frequent usage of the word “son;” the grandson or the nephew of Salathiel.","verses":27,"father":"Pedaiah","mother":"","v":[12,13]},{"id":"shealtiel_2456","name":"Shealtiel","also":"Salathiel","summary":"Asked for of God, father of Zerubbabel (Ezra 3:2, 8; Neh. 12:1).","verses":11,"father":"Jehoiachin","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"azor_559","name":"Azor","also":"","summary":"","verses":2,"father":"Eliakim","mother":"","v":[13,14]},{"id":"abiud_56","name":"Abiud","also":"","summary":"A descendant of Zerubbabel and father of Eliakim (Matt. 1:13, “Abiud”); called also Juda (Luke 3:26), and Obadiah (1 Chr. 3:21).","verses":1,"father":"Zerubbabel","mother":"","v":[13]},{"id":"eliakim_1087","name":"Eliakim","also":"","summary":"The son of Abiud, of the posterity of Zerubbabel (Matt. 1:13).","verses":1,"father":"Abiud","mother":"","v":[13]},{"id":"eliud_1164","name":"Eliud","also":"","summary":"","verses":2,"father":"Achim","mother":"","v":[14,15]},{"id":"achim_65","name":"Achim","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"Sadoc","mother":"","v":[14]},{"id":"sadoc_2454","name":"Sadoc","also":"","summary":"Just, mentioned in the genealogy of our Lord (Matt. 1:14).","verses":1,"father":"Azor","mother":"","v":[14]},{"id":"jacob_683","name":"Jacob","also":"","summary":"","verses":2,"father":"Matthan","mother":"","v":[15,16]},{"id":"eleazar_1069","name":"Eleazar","also":"","summary":"The Second High Priest. Nephew of Moses.","verses":1,"father":"Eliud","mother":"","v":[15]},{"id":"matthan_1968","name":"Matthan","also":"","summary":"The son of Eleazar, and father of Jacob, who was the father of Joseph, the husband of the Virgin Mary (Matt. 1:15).","verses":1,"father":"Eleazar","mother":"","v":[15]},{"id":"mary_1938","name":"Mary","also":"","summary":"The wife of Joseph, the mother of Jesus, called the “Virgin Mary,” though never so designated in Scripture (Matt. 2:11; Acts 1:14). Little is known of her personal history.","verses":21,"father":"Heli","mother":"","v":[16,18,20]},{"id":"joseph_1715","name":"Joseph","also":"","summary":"The foster-father of our Lord (Matt. 1:16; Luke 3:23). He lived at Nazareth in Galilee (Luke 2:4). He is called a “just man.”","verses":15,"father":"Jacob","mother":"","v":[16,18,19,20,24]},{"id":"holy_spirit_7400","name":"Holy Spirit","also":"Comforter, Holy Ghost","summary":"The third Person of the adorable Trinity.","verses":246,"father":"","mother":"","v":[18,20]}],"places":[{"id":"babylon_151","name":"Babylon","kind":"City","lat":32.53617,"lon":44.42082,"summary":"The Greek form of BABEL; Semitic form Babilu, meaning “The Gate of God.” In the Assyrian tablets it means “The city of the dispersion of the tribes.”","verses":255,"v":[11,12,17]}],"events":[{"id":"espousal_of_mary_249","title":"Espousal of Mary","year":-6,"summary":"Passage: Matthew 1:18 – Luke 1:27. People: Mary, Joseph. Place: Nazareth.","v":[18]},{"id":"an_angel_speaks_to_joseph_in_a_dream_253","title":"An Angel Speaks to Joseph in a Dream","year":-5,"summary":"Passage: Matthew 1:19–25. People: Joseph. Place: Nazareth.","v":[19,20,21,22,23,24,25]}],"traditions":[["mary",18,25]],"sources":["Barnes","JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[976,976,976,976,1078,1078,1078,2424,2424,5547,5207,5207,1138,1138,5207,5207,11,11],[11,1080,1080,1080,1080,2464,2464,1080,1080,1080,2384,1161,2384,1080,1080,1080,2455,2532,846,80],[2455,1080,1080,1080,1080,5329,2532,2196,1537,2283,5329,1080,1080,1080,2074,1161,2074,1080,1080,1080,689],[689,1080,1080,1080,1080,284,284,1080,1080,1080,3476,1161,3476,1080,1080,1080,4533],[4533,1080,1080,1080,1080,1003,1537,4477,1003,1080,1080,1080,560